<article> <header class="hero"> <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"> <a href="/">Home</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <a href="/glossary">Glossary</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <span>Straight-through processing (STP)</span> </nav> <div class="hero-badge"><span class="pulse-dot"></span><span style="position:relative;z-index:1">Glossary · Operations</span></div> <h1><span class="accent">Straight-through processing (STP)</span></h1> <p class="page-meta">Glossary entry · Last reviewed 26 July 2026</p> <!-- ANSWER BLOCK — picked up by speakable schema --> <p class="answer-block"><strong>Straight-through processing (STP)</strong> is the automated handling of a payment from initiation to settlement without manual intervention. Unstructured addresses are a leading STP killer; structured addresses enable reliable parsing, validation and screening. Industry cross-border STP baselines sit near <strong>40%</strong>, while ioNova ARS achieves <strong>~98% automatically and &gt;99% with the Exceptions Workbench</strong>.</p> </header> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">In Practice</div> <h2 class="section-title">How Straight-through processing (STP) works in practice</h2> <div class="content-block"><p>The point-of-entry validation shift makes STP the operational battleground: rejected payments no longer queue for downstream repair — they bounce back as exceptions. The EPC’s value statement links structured addresses to error reduction, more accurate screening and better reconciliation, which together drive the higher STP rates.</p></div> <p class="src">Source: the ioNova Postal Address Specification v2.0 glossary (STP); §7.1 Table 12; §8 (EPC value statement); ioNova compare hub (40% → ~98% journey).</p> <div class="content-block"><p>Parent reference: <a href="/address-intelligence/structured-address-value">The business value of structured addresses</a>.</p></div> </section> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">Citations</div> <h2 class="section-title">Sources</h2> <div class="sources-list"> <h3 class="sources-subhead">Standards &amp; regulatory sources</h3>
